From 6da4db1c362137cdce04bab1c9483d4c50ba6879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: sd: add test for read/write range checks

Add a test that runs the SD stack's block read and write calls against a
fake SD host controller, which records the data transfers that reach it.
Ranges within the card must reach the controller; ranges starting at or
running past the end of the card, including ranges whose end wraps past
block 0xffffffff, must be refused with -EINVAL before reaching it.

The existing tests/subsys/sd/sdmmc test only checks that such requests
fail, which a real card does on its own by rejecting the address, so it
cannot tell whether the stack's check worked. This test needs no
hardware and runs on native_sim.
